---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const updated = new Date('2026-08-23');
const updatedLabel = updated.toLocaleDateString('en-GB', {
	year: 'numeric',
	month: 'long',
	day: 'numeric',
});
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Privacy Policy — Luke Coleman"
	description="Privacy policy for iOS apps published by Luke Coleman."
>
	<article class="py-8 pb-16">
		<div class="container-page">
			<header class="mb-8 max-w-2xl border-b border-ink/8 pb-6">
				<p class="mb-3 text-[0.85rem] font-semibold tracking-[0.06em] text-muted uppercase">Legal</p>
				<h1 class="mb-3.5 font-display text-[clamp(2rem,4vw,2.75rem)] leading-tight font-bold tracking-tight">
					Privacy policy
				</h1>
				<p class="mb-3 text-muted">
					This policy applies to iOS apps published by Luke Coleman. Link this page from any App
					Store listing.
				</p>
				<p class="text-[0.9rem] font-semibold text-ink">Last updated: {updatedLabel}</p>
			</header>

			<div
				class="prose prose-neutral max-w-2xl prose-headings:font-display prose-headings:tracking-tight prose-a:text-ink prose-strong:text-ink prose-p:text-muted prose-li:text-muted"
			>
				<h2>Overview</h2>
				<p>
					This Software is provided by <strong>Luke Coleman</strong> (“we”, “us”) and is intended for
					use as is.
				</p>
				<p>
					This page informs visitors about our policies regarding the collection, use, and disclosure
					of personal information if anyone decides to use our iOS apps or related Software (“the
					App” / “our Software”).
				</p>
				<p>
					If you choose to use our Software, you agree to the collection and use of information in
					relation to this policy. Personal information we collect is used for providing and
					improving the Software. We will not use or share your information with anyone except as
					described in this privacy policy.
				</p>

				<h2>Information collection and use</h2>
				<p>
					For a better experience while using our Software, we may require you to provide certain
					personally identifiable information. Information we request will be retained by us and
					used as described in this privacy policy.
				</p>
				<p>
					Our apps may use third-party services that collect information used to identify you.
					Privacy policies of third-party service providers that may be used include:
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li>
						<a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple</a>
					</li>
					<li>
						<a href="https://support.google.com/admob/answer/6128543">AdMob</a>
					</li>
					<li>
						<a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy"
							>Google Analytics for Firebase</a
						>
					</li>
					<li>
						<a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy">Firebase Crashlytics</a>
					</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					Not every app uses every service listed above. Each app only uses the providers it
					integrates.
				</p>

				<h2>Accounts and login</h2>
				<p>
					Unless an app specifically offers sign-up or sign-in, we do not collect usernames,
					passwords, email addresses for accounts, or social login credentials. Where an app does
					offer accounts, we only collect the information needed to create and operate that account,
					as described in the app or at the point of collection.
				</p>

				<h2>In-app purchases</h2>
				<p>If you choose to buy something inside an app:</p>
				<ul>
					<li>
						Payments are processed by the <strong>Apple App Store</strong>, not by us directly.
					</li>
					<li>
						We do <strong>not</strong> receive your full payment card number, bank details, or
						billing address from those purchases.
					</li>
					<li>
						Apple may provide us with limited purchase information (for example, that a product was
						bought or restored) so the app can unlock the paid feature on your device.
					</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					Purchase handling, refunds, and payment data are governed by Apple’s terms and privacy
					policy, in addition to this policy.
				</p>

				<h2>Log data</h2>
				<p>
					Whenever you use our Software, in the case of an error we may collect data and information
					(through third-party products) on your device called Log Data. This Log Data may include
					information such as your device Internet Protocol (“IP”) address, device name, operating
					system version, the configuration of the app when utilizing our Software, the time and date
					of your use of the Software, and other statistics.
				</p>

				<h2>Cookies</h2>
				<p>
					Cookies are files with a small amount of data that are commonly used as anonymous unique
					identifiers. These are sent to your browser from the websites that you visit and are stored
					on your device’s internal memory.
				</p>
				<p>
					Our Software does not use these “cookies” explicitly. However, an app may use third-party
					code and libraries that use cookies to collect information and improve their services. You
					may have the option to accept or refuse cookies. If you refuse cookies, you may not be able
					to use some portions of the Software.
				</p>

				<h2>Service providers</h2>
				<p>We may employ third-party companies and individuals to:</p>
				<ul>
					<li>Facilitate our Software</li>
					<li>Provide the Software on our behalf</li>
					<li>Perform Software-related services</li>
					<li>Assist us in analyzing how our Software is used</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					These third parties may have access to your personal information to perform tasks assigned
					to them on our behalf. They are obligated not to disclose or use the information for any
					other purpose.
				</p>
				<p>
					We rely on <strong>Apple</strong> (App Store / StoreKit) for iOS distribution and
					purchases. Apple processes related data under its own privacy policy. We do not sell your
					personal information.
				</p>

				<h2>Security</h2>
				<p>
					We value your trust in providing us your personal information and strive to use
					commercially acceptable means of protecting it. No method of transmission over the
					internet, or method of electronic storage, is 100% secure and reliable, and we cannot
					guarantee its absolute security.
				</p>

				<h2>Data stored on your device</h2>
				<p>
					Purchase or entitlement status, preferences, and other app data may be stored locally on
					your device (and/or managed by the App Store) so features work as expected. That
					information stays on your device and with Apple unless you remove the app or clear related
					data according to your device settings, or unless a feature below states that data is sent
					for processing.
				</p>

				<h2>Cloud or AI processing</h2>
				<p>
					When an app offers AI or cloud-powered effects, the selected content may be sent securely
					to our servers or to trusted third-party AI providers solely to generate the requested
					result. That content is used only for the processing task. It is not retained afterward for
					training or shared beyond what is needed to provide the feature. Providers used for a given
					feature (if any) are disclosed in the app or related materials.
				</p>

				<h2>Links to other sites</h2>
				<p>
					Our Software may contain links to other sites. If you click a third-party link, you will be
					directed to that site. Those external sites are not operated by us. We strongly advise you
					to review the privacy policy of those websites. We have no control over and assume no
					responsibility for the content, privacy policies, or practices of any third-party sites or
					services.
				</p>

				<h2>Children’s privacy</h2>
				<p>
					Our Software does not address anyone under the age of 13. We do not knowingly collect
					personally identifiable information from children under 13. If we discover that a child
					under 13 has provided us with personal information, we will delete it from our servers. If
					you are a parent or guardian and you are aware that your child has provided us with
					personal information, please contact us so we can take appropriate action.
				</p>

				<h2>Changes to this privacy policy</h2>
				<p>
					We may update this privacy policy from time to time. You are advised to review this page
					periodically for any changes. We will notify you of changes by posting the new privacy
					policy on this page. Continued use of our Software after changes means you accept the
					updated policy.
				</p>

				<h2>Contact us</h2>
				<p>
					If you have any questions or suggestions about this privacy policy, contact us at
					<a href="mailto:hello@lukeacoleman.dev">hello@lukeacoleman.dev</a>.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</article>
</BaseLayout>
